<section class="v31-offers" data-editorial id="approach" aria-labelledby="first-step">
  <header class="section-head"><p class="kicker">Three ways to work with us</p><h2 id="first-step">Start with a decision. Continue into a build.</h2></header>
  <div class="engagement-tiers" id="engagements">
    <article class="engagement-tier" id="review" aria-labelledby="review-title">
      <h3 id="review-title">Decision Review</h3><p class="tier-price">€14,000<span>Fixed fee</span></p><p class="tier-duration"><strong>4 weeks</strong><span>8–10 interviews in total</span></p>
      <p class="tier-for">For a decision with a date: whether to launch a first builder cohort, change a programme that already runs, or hire someone to own it.</p>
      <ul><li>Interviews with your team and external participants, supported by existing records.</li><li>Evidence of what builders need and what your team can support.</li><li>Costed options and one recommendation with a named owner.</li></ul>
      <ul class="first-step-outcomes tier-decision" aria-label="The decision"><li><span class="glyph glyph-circle" aria-hidden="true"></span>Go ahead</li><li><span class="glyph glyph-square" aria-hidden="true"></span>Change course</li><li><span class="glyph glyph-triangle" aria-hidden="true"></span>Hold off</li></ul>
      <p class="tier-next">The Review is the first phase of the Programme Build. Continue with an agreed scope for a further €28,000.</p>
      <div class="tier-actions"><a class="text-link" href="#talk">Discuss a decision <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </article>
    <article class="engagement-tier engagement-tier-programme" id="build" aria-labelledby="build-title">
      <h3 id="build-title">Programme Build</h3><p class="tier-price">€42,000<span>Fixed fee, with one stop gate</span></p><p class="tier-duration"><strong>13 weeks</strong><span>Includes the 4-week Review</span></p>
      <p class="tier-for">For one change with a launch date: a path to a first useful build, a first builder cohort, a route for integrations, or a change to a programme that already runs.</p>
      <ol class="tier-path" aria-label="How the Build runs and is paid">
        <li><span class="tier-path-amount">€14,000 to start</span><span class="tier-path-weeks">Weeks 1–4</span>The Decision Review.</li>
        <li class="tier-path-gate"><span class="tier-path-amount">Stop gate</span>Stop here and keep the decision, or approve the build.</li>
        <li><span class="tier-path-amount">€28,000 to continue</span><span class="tier-path-weeks">Weeks 5–13</span>Two €14,000 instalments, at weeks 5 and 10. Detailed design, launch, initial use, one adjustment and handover.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="tier-followup">Includes one progress review 90 days after handover, based on your team’s reports.</p>
      <div class="tier-actions"><a class="text-link" href="#talk">Discuss a build <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </article>
    <article class="engagement-tier engagement-tier-custom" id="support" aria-labelledby="support-title">
      <h3 id="support-title">Programme Support</h3><p class="tier-price tier-price-custom">Custom<span>Scoped to your programmes</span></p><p class="tier-duration"><strong>Ongoing</strong><span>Monthly, agreed in writing</span></p>
      <p class="tier-for">For teams launching or running programmes who want senior support alongside their own staff.</p>
      <ul><li>Launch support for new programmes and changes to existing ones.</li><li>Regular working sessions with the people who run them.</li><li>Priorities and progress reviewed with your sponsor.</li></ul>
      <div class="tier-actions"><a class="text-link" href="#talk">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="engagement-expect"><strong>What to expect.</strong> You provide a sponsor who approves decisions and an operator who runs the work. When you continue past the stop gate, the Build ends with the change launched, in use and handed over to your team. Fees exclude VAT.</p>
  <details class="engagement-scope"><summary>Scope, access, responsibilities and exclusions</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Decision Review:</strong> one decision, its owner and the person who approves the spend; 8–10 interviews in total; interviewee introductions by day 3, data and tool access by day 5; the approver joins the decision session. €14,000 at kickoff.</li>
      <li><strong>Programme Build:</strong> one intervention for one primary audience; a named sponsor and an operator with about four hours a week from week 5; approvals within five working days. €14,000 at kickoff; after the week-4 stop gate, €28,000 invoiced as €14,000 at week 5 and €14,000 at week 10.</li>
      <li><strong>Builder cohort:</strong> one contribution track and a small group of builders. We select the builders with you, speak with each of them, shape the cohort with them and your team, support the first cycle and hand it over. Your operator runs the cohort day to day, and an engineer on your team reviews contributions and answers technical questions while it runs. Credits or payments to participants are your cost.</li>
      <li><strong>Delays:</strong> if client-side delays push a phase past its planned end, we re-plan on dates agreed with our availability, and agree any remobilisation work before resuming.</li>
      <li><strong>Progress review:</strong> one session ninety days after handover, based on what your team reports, with a short note. It does not prove lasting impact.</li>
      <li><strong>Programme Support:</strong> scope, cadence, fees and term agreed in writing before work starts.</li>
      <li><strong>Not included:</strong> ongoing operation or moderation, software builds beyond configuring existing tools, event production, paid media, travel, third-party costs and hiring outcomes.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>
</section>
